    "sha": "174da2b81debe7fc80c4ad97cecb95f18903e9dd",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDE3NGRhMmI4MWRlYmU3ZmM4MGM0YWQ5N2NlY2I5NWYxODkwM2U5ZGQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-19T07:20:02Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-19T07:20:02Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): rate a hole op by the lower of the material row and the running feed\n\nA Drill or Thread op is now rated by the lower of two values when the\nmaterial in force on its setup is the document's material: the tool's\ncutting-data row for that material, and the tool's running feed. Before,\na running feed lowered below a row that names the material did not reach\nthe rating, so an op at the row feed posted with no refusal.\n\nThe seed of a new or retargeted Drill or Thread op uses the same rating,\nso a seeded op is never refused by the post check. A stock that states\nits own material keeps the rating of its own row.\n\nPinned by hole_feed_rating::a_running_feed_lowered_below_the_material_row_is_the_rating.\n\nFixes #2724\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
